@startuml
title Figure 5: System Administrator - Department Management & System Reports

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam dpi 150
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "System\nAdministrator" as Admin
participant "System" as System
database "Database" as DB
participant "Report\nGenerator" as Report

== Department Management ==

Admin -> System: Create Department\n(Name, Description)
System -> DB: Check Department Exists\n(Name)
DB --> System: Not Found
System -> DB: INSERT INTO departments\n(name, description, isActive=true)
DB --> System: Department Created\n(Department ID)
System --> Admin: Department Created\nSuccessfully

Admin -> System: View All Departments
System -> DB: SELECT * FROM departments\nWHERE isActive=true
DB --> System: Department List
System --> Admin: Display Departments\n(Name, Description, HOD)

Admin -> System: Update Department\n(Name, Description)
System -> DB: UPDATE departments\nSET description
DB --> System: Department Updated
System --> Admin: Department Updated\nSuccessfully

== System Reports ==

Admin -> System: Generate System Report\n(Date Range, Filters)
System -> DB: SELECT issues, users,\ndepartments statistics
DB --> System: Aggregated Data\n(Total Issues, By Status,\nBy Department, By Priority)
System -> Report: Generate Report\n(PDF/Excel/CSV/Word)
Report -> Report: Create Charts\n(Pie, Bar, Line)
Report -> Report: Format Tables\n(Issue Details)
Report -> Report: Add RRA Logo\n& Header
Report --> System: Report File Generated
System --> Admin: Download Report\n(report.pdf)

Admin -> System: View Audit Logs\n(Filter by User/Action)
System -> DB: SELECT * FROM audit_logs\nWHERE filters
DB --> System: Audit Log Records\n(User, Action, Timestamp,\nIP Address)
System --> Admin: Display Audit Logs\n(Searchable Table)

Admin -> System: View All Issues\n(All Departments)
System -> DB: SELECT * FROM issues\nORDER BY created_at DESC
DB --> System: All Issues\n(Cross-Department)
System --> Admin: Display Issues\n(Read-Only View)

Admin -> System: Add Comment to Issue\n(Issue ID, Comment)
System -> DB: INSERT INTO issue_comments\n(issue_id, user_id, content)
DB --> System: Comment Added
System -> DB: INSERT notification\n(For Issue Owner)
System --> Admin: Comment Added\nSuccessfully

@enduml
